 "marks": [
  {
   "d": "2021-11-03",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY21",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "Operationally, we are seeing improving market conditions and activity levels in all our geographies, albeit at different speeds, with Germany bouncing back strongly, France performing well and an encouraging recovery in the UK.",
   "file": "20211103_CLI_Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-08-10",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "The economic, geopolitical and market situation and outlook have deteriorated markedly since the end of the first quarter with the impact of the Russian invasion of Ukraine contributing to existing inflationary and supply chain pressures.",
   "file": "20220810_CLI_Half-year-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2022-11-16",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY22",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "CLS remains on course with its plans for the year with earnings tracking in-line with market expectations[1].",
   "file": "20221116_CLI_Q3-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-08-09",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "As expected, the economic backdrop for the property market has been challenging and we expect it to remain so until interest rates have definitively peaked.",
   "file": "20230809_CLI_Half-year-Report.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2023-11-15",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY23",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "Consequently, the Board remains confident that the Group will meet its earnings expectations for the full year.",
   "file": "20231115_CLI_Q3-Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-08-07",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 1,
   "q": "There are signs of improvements in the real estate investment market and leasing activity continues to be positive as occupiers are increasingly prepared to commit to the right locations and buildings.",
   "file": "20240807_CLI_CLS-Holdings-Half-Year-Report.md",
   "gnote": "early signal: first step up in tone"
  },
  {
   "d": "2024-11-13",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -2,
   "q": "The letting trend remains positive although we are experiencing longer decision timelines due to macro and political factors slowing progress.",
   "file": "20241113_CLI_Trading-Update-12-November-2024.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-02-24",
   "doc": "YE-TU",
   "fy": "FY24",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "We expect CLS' 2024 EPRA earnings and Net Tangible Assets (\"NTA\") to be in line with market expectations[1] when we publish our 2024 full year accounts at the end of March 2025.",
   "file": "20250224_CLI_Trading-Update-24-February-2025.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-08-13",
   "doc": "H1 R",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": 0,
   "q": "The occupational market remains healthy and is showing signs of improvement with increased take-up in the UK and Germany, our two biggest markets, which bodes well for CLS to capture the significant earnings upside from reducing vacancy",
   "file": "20250813_CLI_Half-Yearly-Results-Announcement-2025.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2025-12-02",
   "doc": "Q3 TU",
   "fy": "FY25",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "In the first three quarters of 2025, CLS' transaction levels remained resilient, with letting activity in-line with 2024, albeit with lower activity than was initially targeted, from the continued economic and political backdrop across our countries, with the UK particularly noteworthy.",
   "file": "20251202_CLI_Trading-Update.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2026-03-13",
   "doc": "FY R",
   "fy": "FY26",
   "g": "flat",
   "s": -1,
   "q": "It is early days and therefore difficult to judge the short- and longer-term impact of the war on Europe's economies and, therefore, property markets.",
   "file": "20260313_CLI_Annual-Financial-Results.md"
  },
  {
   "d": "2026-08-04",
   "doc": "H1 TU",
   "fy": "FY26",
   "g": "CUT",
   "s": -3,
   "q": "As such, the Board now expects 2026 full year EPS to be in the range of 4.6 to 5.5 pence per share*.",
   "file": "20260804_CLI_Trading-Update.md"
